WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.670
From secret time-travel machines to classic
horror movie references and the hidden truth

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:10.120
about Christopher the cube, the third season
of The Umbrella Academy is loaded with tons

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.530
of weird and wonderful details you might have
missed.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:17.400
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and these
are the biggest and best Umbrella Academy

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.369
easter eggs hidden in Season 3.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:21.579
Spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:21.579 --> 00:00:26.070
The little dog at the hotel's reception desk
with the nametag "Mr Pennycrumb", who goes

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:30.400
missing in one of the Kugelblitz waves, is
a nod to the comics where Five has a canine

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.399
companion with the same name, who in turn
was named after Umbrella Academy co-creator

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:37.829
Gabriel Bá's real-life pug.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:42.270
When Klaus sneaks back into the Sparrow Academy,
the film he watches with Reginald…

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.379
I love this movie.
…is The Hunchback of Notre Dame.

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:50.070
Several characters in the movie get literally
stabbed in the back, which is why Reginald

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.110
says:
Never turn your back, my boy.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.000
Especially not to your children.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.539
Reginald's comment foreshadows his own demise
at the hands of Allison, who strikes him from

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:03.840
behind to stop him harming her siblings any
further, but it also telegraphs his betrayal

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.780
of Klaus who he metaphorically stabs in the
back by shutting him in the Hotel Obsidian

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.160
as it gets Kugelblitzed…

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.120
You've done a fine job bringing me back into
the family fold.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.980
You're just more trouble than you're worth.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:20.310
And Reginald's words 'Never turn your back'
also foreshadow Klaus's death as he literally

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.731
stabs himself in the back by launching himself
onto the horns of the white buffalo, which

00:01:24.731 --> 00:01:28.610
also brings to mind Pogo's death in season
1.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:33.050
In the season's opening scene on the subway,
there's an easter egg to a breakfast cereal

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:37.120
called Clever Crisp, which Reginald Hargreeves
invented in the comics.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.020
It also made an appearance in Season 2 on
the kitchen table in Elliot's home.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:46.410
And there was also an ad for the cereal outside
the store Klaus steals from in the first season.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:49.180
There's another neat detail in that scene
as well.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.500
Notice how the Korean girl about to give birth
to a super-baby is positioned just in front

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.920
of a seat sign for pregnant women, foreshadowing
what's about to happen next.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.570
And when the camera moves round and she repositions
herself to avoid a kiss from her boyfriend,

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:07.250
they perfectly frame the pregnant woman and
woman with child sign in the shot.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.420
This scene also mirrors the Season 1 cold
open with a Russian girl, where her boyfriend

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.570
also goes to kiss her and she pulls away before
kissing him then running off.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.990
And there's a call-back to that same pilot
episode scene when the Umbrella team look

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.340
through newspaper clippings about their mothers
and find one about a young woman who died

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.170
after kissing her boyfriend then jumping into
a swimming pool.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:32.950
Just before Stanley gets Kugelblitzed, he's
drinking a slushee, and when he bites the

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:37.950
dust, his drink container hits the floor revealing
a comic-book image of the Umbrella Academy's

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.950
Number 2.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.760
All of which happens as Diego looks on in
the background of the shot.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.630
Hidden away on a lower level at the Sparrow
Academy is Five's backpack from the third

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.290
series of the comics which is called The Hotel
Oblivion.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.230
Also in this shot is a black and white photo
of two kids hugging each other.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.740
It's been deliberately placed on a desk next
to various beakers and test tubes and there's

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.180
a blackboard behind with formulas and notes
scrawled on it.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.430
This could be a clue to the origins of the
cube and Sparrow member known as Christopher,

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:13.319
implying he was originally a human boy, as
I suggested in my Season 2 Harlan theory video.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:17.840
Now we've seen season 3, it could be that
Christopher was critically injured on a mission

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.270
and Hargreaves decided the only way for him
to survive was to save his consciousness by

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.630
placing it inside a cube.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:28.190
Hargreaves did a similar thing with Luther
when he was on the verge of death by injecting

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.540
him with a serum that turned him into a half-human,
half-ape.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.840
Likewise, in the superhero show Doom Patrol,
after a terrible accident, the brain of Cliff

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.470
Steele was salvaged from his body and placed
inside a robot.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:45.319
The Umbrella family dancing together during
the opening episode's Footloose sequence creates

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:49.750
a nice parallel with the pilot where they
all danced separately to I Think We're Alone

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
Now.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.860
And there's a call-back to that very first
dance with Luther busting out some of his

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:54.959
old moves.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:58.770
Grace – appropriately for her character
– does the robot and she does it while dancing

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.819
with Diego which seems pretty fitting given
how close he is to his mum.

00:04:02.819 --> 00:04:07.940
Speaking of family ties, Ben and Klaus also
dance together in a nod to OG Ben and Klaus's

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.090
close connection.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:14.130
There's also some foreshadowing of Luther's
season 3 romance as his main doubles dance

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.130
is with Sloane.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:19.759
And there's a little throw-back to his romantic
season 1 dance with Allison when he ends his

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.779
dance with Sloane by twirling her around.

00:04:22.779 --> 00:04:28.030
The cast also perform plenty of moves from
the original Footloose dance in the 1984 musical

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.030
movie.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.930
And there's more shout-outs to the 80s film
in Christopher's glitter drop, the balloons

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:37.029
around the floor, and the way they all circle
around and watch as different dancers take

00:04:37.029 --> 00:04:38.159
their turn to shine.

00:04:38.159 --> 00:04:42.689
Plus, given how specific showrunner Steve
Blackman is in his choice of music for the

00:04:42.689 --> 00:04:47.830
series, and how he writes songs into the script,
the Footloose lyrics about 'working so hard'

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:52.289
and wondering why you bother fit the Umbrellas'
current situation pretty well, given they

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:55.889
saved the world only to find their father's
replaced them.

00:04:55.889 --> 00:04:59.569
And then there's the line: 'I've got this
feeling that time's just holding me down',

00:04:59.569 --> 00:05:02.500
another perfect fit for our time-travelling
team.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.729
One of this season's main locations, the Hotel,
has strong echoes of The Shining.

00:05:07.729 --> 00:05:10.689
The way Klaus introduces his siblings to the
place…

00:05:10.689 --> 00:05:14.039
Back in her heyday, she played host to world
leaders.

00:05:14.039 --> 00:05:16.889
…mirrors the way the Torrance family are
shown around The Overlook Hotel:

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:19.490
In its heyday, it was one of the stopping
places for the jetset.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.809
They had four presidents who stayed here.

00:05:22.809 --> 00:05:27.189
Then there's the wallpaper in Harlan's room
and again at the Barber's, which has the same

00:05:27.189 --> 00:05:31.130
distinctive geometric pattern as the famous
Shining carpet.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:35.949
Also, soon after the siblings settle into
their rooms, we get a real grown-up Grady

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:40.770
sisters meets Grey Gardens vibe in this shot
of two women in the hallway, each holding

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.300
white cats.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:47.340
And let's not forget the whole claustrophobic,
maze-like feel of the hotel, where we see

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:50.900
the Umbrella team repeatedly lose themselves
and each other.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.590
It's like the thing is alive.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:57.680
It's interesting also how Five talks about
the hotel being alive and Klaus anthropomorphises

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.180
it too…

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.389
Absorb her into your bosom.
…because among the many popular theories

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:07.330
about The Shining is one that says its hotel
possesses Jack, absorbing his soul.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:12.129
And, given this season's many hat-tips to
Stanley Kubrick's The Shining movie, it seems

00:06:12.129 --> 00:06:18.669
particularly apt that the boy who Lila introduces
in the hotel as Diego's son shares the director's

00:06:18.669 --> 00:06:20.310
name:
Diego, meet Stan.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.539
Say hello, Stanley!

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:26.369
There's a real ring of Alfred Hitchcock's
60s horror film The Birds throughout the season,

00:06:26.369 --> 00:06:31.129
for example, when Fei's ravens crowd round
then chase Luther in the park, and also in

00:06:31.129 --> 00:06:35.339
the first episode when they pursue Luther
and Allison through the Academy then peck

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:37.469
down the door they hide behind.

00:06:37.469 --> 00:06:42.369
I love the way the birds emerge from Fei's
back, almost like wings, and return there

00:06:42.369 --> 00:06:48.189
after their work is done, and notice how Fei's
bird-like tendencies even extend to how she

00:06:48.189 --> 00:06:49.189
eats.

00:06:49.189 --> 00:06:53.129
On top of that, there are definite shades
of Morpheus from The Matrix in Fei's look

00:06:53.129 --> 00:06:54.669
in this scene.

00:06:54.669 --> 00:06:59.860
Interestingly, both Klaus and Luther's deaths
are foreshadowed in the opening episode when,

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.280
after the Umbrellas' battle with the Sparrows,
Diego runs into Reginald's office and tells

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.349
his brother:
You're probably gonna die.

00:07:06.349 --> 00:07:08.809
And then the scene cuts straight to Luther.

00:07:08.809 --> 00:07:13.939
Later on, when Luther and co empty their pockets
to pay for their hotel stay, Klaus brings

00:07:13.939 --> 00:07:19.289
out a bunch of condoms, and one of the brands
is Valhalla, also the name of the fifth episode

00:07:19.289 --> 00:07:20.310
of Season 2.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:24.130
A few episodes later Luther also buys the
same brand…

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.130
Condoms?

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.249
For sex.
[both chuckle]

00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:27.689
Which is a thing I do now.

00:07:27.689 --> 00:07:32.869
Now, in Norse mythology, Valhalla is a place
in the afterlife for slain warriors.

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:37.939
And both he and Klaus end up later on in the
Void, the show's version of Heaven or the

00:07:37.939 --> 00:07:38.939
afterlife.

00:07:38.939 --> 00:07:43.410
Plus, notice when Luther asks for condoms,
how the seller goes to get the 'regular' size

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:48.179
at first, then looks downwards and picks up
an 'extra large' pack instead.

00:07:48.179 --> 00:07:52.729
When Lila tries to use a briefcase to travel
to Berlin, she's carrying a record with an

00:07:52.729 --> 00:07:57.310
ape on the cover by a group called Prime8s,
a hat-tip to the comics where where Number

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:00.330
2 and 7 have a punk band together called the
Prime-8's.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:04.789
The group's name fits well in the world of
both the show and comics which each have their

00:08:04.789 --> 00:08:11.029
share of simian characters, but it also feels
like a play on the virtual band Gorillaz.

00:08:11.029 --> 00:08:16.340
Five gets his very own Michael Corleone moment
when he and Lila return to the Commission:

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.490
You know, Lila, I shouldn't even be here.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.490
I was out.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.920
I was done, and yet here I am, swept back
into the chaos.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.740
…which the second I heard it, reminded me
of Michael's famous line from the final film

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:31.259
in the Godfather trilogy: Just when I thought
I was out, they pulled me back in.

00:08:31.259 --> 00:08:35.899
In Reginald's office, there's a photo of him
next to the Eiffel Tower, an easter egg to

00:08:35.899 --> 00:08:40.490
the comics where the Umbrella Academy have
to save Paris when the city's famous tower

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.149
starts killing people.

00:08:42.149 --> 00:08:46.459
In the books, the tower is actually a spaceship
operated by Gustave Eiffel.

00:08:46.459 --> 00:08:50.920
There were also a couple of shout-outs to
the team's Eiffel Tower mission in season

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:55.720
1 via a framed newspaper cutting in Reginald's
study and when Allison's daughter Claire begged:

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:56.720
One more story, Mommy.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.290
I wanna hear the one about the Eiffel Tower.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.910
And after their successful mission in Paris,
the Umbrella team were rewarded with ice cream,

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:09.481
as also happens on other occasions too, and
there's a nod to that in the 'Papa's Soft

00:09:09.481 --> 00:09:13.690
Serve' poster outside the diner where Viktor
is trying to depower Harlan.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:18.250
And there's another soft-serve moment when
Klaus uses an ice cream metaphor to try and

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:22.769
describe how he feels to Reginald:
I feel like scoop after scoop's been taken

00:09:22.769 --> 00:09:23.769
out of me.

00:09:23.769 --> 00:09:24.920
Do you want some ice cream?

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.210
Would that shut you up?

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:31.649
Which also brings to mind Klaus's iconic ice-cream
truck moment from Season 1.

00:09:31.649 --> 00:09:36.310
Just before Reginald kills Luther, he says:
The best way to bring a family together is

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:37.720
at a wedding or a funeral.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:42.699
Of course, he's talking about Luther's recent
wedding to Sloane and now his imminent death.

00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:47.720
But this moment is also a throw-back to the
pilot episode, the title of which is 'We Only

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.019
See Each Other at Weddings and Funerals',
and where it was Reginald's own funeral that

00:09:52.019 --> 00:09:54.269
brought the Umbrella siblings back together.

00:09:54.269 --> 00:09:59.340
So, it's ironic that their father is now using
his son's death to bring the family together

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:02.440
again for his own purposes at the end of season
3.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:07.940
There's an interesting parallel between two
songs about heroes in the first and last episodes.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:12.459
The first one "No More Heroes" by The Stranglers,
hits the nail on the head as the Umbrellas

00:10:12.459 --> 00:10:16.430
lose their fight against the Sparrows, who've
usurped them at the Academy.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:20.770
While the second, The Heavy's "Short-Change
Hero", with its repeated line 'This ain't

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:25.779
no place for no hero', fits the fact that
the Umbrella crew no longer have their powers,

00:10:25.779 --> 00:10:31.000
and as the camera swoops upwards to billionaire
Reginald Hargreeves in his towering offices,

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.430
the line 'This ain't no place for no better
man' seems doubly fitting.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:40.160
When Marcus wanders down to the Academy basement,
there's another comic-book easter egg in the

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.110
form of a sign for a Televator.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:46.480
In the comics, the Televator is a machine
invented by Reginald Hargreeves to travel

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:51.850
through space, time, and across dimensions
and Klaus has one built to transport him,

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:54.000
Diego, and Luther from Vietnam to Dallas.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.680
There was also a reference to the device on
a comic-book cover in Season 1, and there

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:02.980
were plans for the Televator on Reginald's
blackboard in his hidden research room in

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:03.980
Season 2.

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:08.199
In fact, I think this Televator easter egg
that keeps appearing through all the seasons

00:11:08.199 --> 00:11:13.079
could be a big clue that Reginald is using
the machine to loop through time over and

00:11:13.079 --> 00:11:18.089
over, something I explain in more detail in
my Season 3 explained and Season 4 theories

00:11:18.089 --> 00:11:19.089
video.

00:11:19.089 --> 00:11:22.380
Tap here to watch that or there's a link in
the video description below.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:27.209
A bonus detail you might have missed in the
mid-credits scene is this little QR code next

00:11:27.209 --> 00:11:28.209
to Ben.

00:11:28.209 --> 00:11:32.700
If you scan it, it'll take you to a webpage
set up by Netflix for Pogo's Tattoo Shop.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:36.930
At the moment, you can get a digital set of
tattoos with various symbols and easter eggs

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:37.930
from the show.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:42.139
If you can't get the code to scan on your
phone, just go the website on screen here.

00:11:42.139 --> 00:11:46.949
So, Movie Lovers, what other details and easter
eggs did you notice in season 3?

00:11:46.949 --> 00:11:49.220
Let me know in the comments below.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:54.950
Tap here for my full explanation of that cliffhanger
ending and what to expect in Season 4.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:58.540
And if you liked this video, do leave a thumbs-up,
I really appreciate it.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:03.310
Thanks for enjoying The Umbrella Academy with
me and hope you have a marvellous movie-loving

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.310
week!

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:05.540
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

